<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Data-drive check: a LaunchDaemon that runs every 60 s, from boot, with no login needed.

  WHY: the server runs in a container and cannot see whether macOS mounted the SSD. This job runs
  check-data-drive.sh on the host and writes deploy/state/host.json. The server reads that file,
  and "kterm-server status" reports a missing, read-only or nearly full drive (or a report that
  is more than 5 minutes old).

  BEFORE YOU START (on the Mac Studio):
    1. "init" has run, so deploy/state/ exists (init creates it).
    2. The SSD is mounted. Find its path with:  ls /Volumes   (for example /Volumes/KalshiData).
       DRIVE_PATH must be the mount point itself, not a folder inside it. A plain folder on the
       boot disk fails the mount test; see the comments in check-data-drive.sh for the option
       that accepts one.
    3. Use absolute paths. launchd does not expand ~ or $HOME.

  INSTALL (copy and paste; set your own two values on the second line):
    cd /Users/YOU/KalshiTerm2/deploy
    DEPLOY_DIR="$PWD"; DRIVE_PATH=/Volumes/KalshiData
    sed -e "s|__DEPLOY_DIR__|$DEPLOY_DIR|g" -e "s|__DRIVE_PATH__|$DRIVE_PATH|g" \
        host/com.kalshiterm.hostcheck.plist.template \
      | sudo tee /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.hostcheck.plist >/dev/null
    sudo chown root:wheel /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.hostcheck.plist
    sudo chmod 644 /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.hostcheck.plist
    sudo launchctl bootstrap system /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.hostcheck.plist
  macOS may show a "background item added" notification; that is expected.

  VERIFY (within a minute):
    cat state/host.json     "mounted" and "writable" should be true; "checked_at" is recent
    docker compose exec ingest kterm-server status     the "host drive" problem is gone

  TROUBLESHOOTING:
    "Bootstrap failed: 5: Input/output error": it is already loaded, or the file is not
      root:wheel with mode 644. Run the bootout line below, fix the file, bootstrap again.
    No state/host.json: run the script once by hand and read its output:
      sudo host/check-data-drive.sh "$DRIVE_PATH" state/host.json
      Also check that it is executable:  ls -l host/check-data-drive.sh
    "mounted": false although the SSD is attached: DRIVE_PATH is wrong or is not the mount point.
    After editing the file: bootout, then bootstrap again.

  REMOVE:
    sudo launchctl bootout system/com.kalshiterm.hostcheck
    sudo rm /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.kalshiterm.hostcheck.plist
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.kalshiterm.hostcheck</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__DEPLOY_DIR__/host/check-data-drive.sh</string>
    <string>__DRIVE_PATH__</string>
    <string>__DEPLOY_DIR__/state/host.json</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>60</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
